: middle;&quot; /&gt;45 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;10&lt;br&gt;Coloring algorithms for sparse Jacobian and Hessian matrices&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/JuliaDecisionFocusedLearning/CoolPDLP.jl&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CoolPDLP.jl&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;14 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;3&lt;br&gt;A pure-Julia, hardware-agnostic parallel implementation of Primal-Dual hybrid gradient for Linear Programming (PDLP) and its variants.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Hi there 👋&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I am a researcher in applied mathematics at École des Ponts (&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.lvmt.fr/&quot;&gt;LVMT&lt;/a&gt;). My main specialties are machine learning and optimization, with a focus on applications to transport and logistics. Before that, I was a postdoc at EPFL (&lt;a href=&quot;https://indy.epfl.ch/&quot;&gt;INDY&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.epfl.ch/labs/idephics/&quot;&gt;IdePHICS&lt;/a&gt;) and a visiting student at MIT (&lt;a href=&quot;https://julia.mit.edu/&quot;&gt;Julia lab&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A large part of my work is devoted to open-source scientific software in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://julialang.org/&quot;&gt;Julia programming language&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/anuraghazra/github-readme-stats&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://github-readme-stats.vercel.app/api?username=gdalle&quot; alt=&quot;gdalle&#39;s GitHub stats&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
